     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.1 scale 4-[SDGs integrated in the mandate of existing coordination structures and new structures established including NEC sub-committee on SDGs. The project reported regularly to provide updates to NEC Sub-committee on SDGs] 
1.2: Scale 4- [SDG Action plan/frameworks at national/sub-national level established and development plans are partially SDGs aligned. 7 publications related to SDGs were disseminated facilitating alignment of provincial strategies with SDGs including Balochistan Comprehensive Development Growth Strategy (2021-2026); SDGs and Islam; Green Building and Design Standards; SDG Costing for Balochistan; Provincial SDG Framework for Balochistan; and District Localization Plans for Nushki and Killa Abdullah]. 
1.3: Scale 4: [Stakeholders have a greater understanding of SDGs, the project undertook advocacy around SDGs through district SDG awareness sessions engaging district administration and local stakeholders around SDGs, engagement with academia, and other key stakeholders including provincial commission on status of women. The project also conducted radio shows for SDG advocacy].
1.4: Scale 3 [Private sector partially engaged in SDG implementation. The project engaged with BOI and introduced it to SDG Investments &amp; Climate Financing Facility]. 
2.1: Scale-3-P [Baselines and targets established for prioritized SDG indicators]. 
2.2: scale 3-P [Reasonable understanding and knowledge on SDGs monitoring and reporting. In 2022, the provincial BoS and P&amp;DD participated in workshops on knowledge sharing on monitoring and reporting on SDGs. For 2023, in the next phase of the project, capacity building on BoS will be further strengthened on SDG monitoring and reporting].
3.1: Scale 2-P [Performance based criteria established but not fully used for resource allocation at national/ sub-national level].
4.1 Scale-3- [Innovative approaches were fully established for SDG implementation. The project in 2022 
 provided e-commerce training to 100 students (including 30 women),and organized a challenge cup to promote innovation on SDG implementation amongst university students].</narrative>
      </comment>
